(1561841, 208322, 34192, '<td valign="top">One of the criteria for this challenge is "Creativity is the Key" so my scoring will be based on this.  Love the colorful nature of this image.  Not too hot on the stone wall but you take what you can get.  The buildings look like they curve - not sure if thats true but if its not, I probably would have gotten closer to the the left to show a little more perspective.  I believe this image is one of the more creative ones in the challenge.  The focus is good, POV okay, DOF well done, lighting okay.  7 - good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'One of the criteria for this challenge is "Creativity is the Key" so my scoring will be based on this.  Love the colorful nature of this image.  Not too hot on the stone wall but you take what you can get.  The buildings look like they curve - not sure if thats true but if its not, I probably would have gotten closer to the the left to show a little more perspective.  I believe this image is one of the more creative ones in the challenge.  The focus is good, POV okay, DOF well done, lighting okay.  7 - good luck in the challenge!', '2005-07-25 14:58:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1561850, 206295, 40355, '<td valign="top">The violin fairly glows in this shot.  Well done!</td>', 'The violin fairly glows in this shot.  Well done!', '2005-07-25 15:01:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1561851, 208112, 34192, '<td valign="top">One of the criteria for this challenge is "Creativity is the Key" so my scoring will be based on this.  I like the various textures in this.  I like that it was not shot head on but slightly off to the right.  Could have cropped a little off the bottom - the green of the grass doesn''t do much for me.  Like the competing shapes, that the darkness of the window is balanced by the extra number of barrels.  I think the lighting is good for the subject.  Not thrilled about the top but not sure it should be cut off -  think something would be lost if it was.  very well done. 7 - good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'One of the criteria for this challenge is "Creativity is the Key" so my scoring will be based on this.  I like the various textures in this.  I like that it was not shot head on but slightly off to the right.  Could have cropped a little off the bottom - the green of the grass doesn''t do much for me.  Like the competing shapes, that the darkness of the window is balanced by the extra number of barrels.  I think the lighting is good for the subject.  Not thrilled about the top but not sure it should be cut off -  think something would be lost if it was.  very well done. 7 - good luck in the challenge!', '2005-07-25 15:02:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1561854, 208632, 38492, '<td valign="top">The chair is too tighlty cropped at the top - it is better to show it all than lose only a tiny part of it to the edge. Quite a bright day - the highlights are excessive - there are two points of glare on the seat, and two on the rear. Shooting on a cloudier day, or at a different time of day so the sunlight isn''t so harsh would help. There is a lot of detail in here, but I would have preferred a deeper DoF - the rear table leg also deserves to be in focus.<br/>Nice use of the table to provide great leading linse, but they don''t lead to anything! Maybe If you rotated the chair clockwise, so we could see the detail on the front rather than the side, it would help. Another minor distraction is the top of the far char intersecting with the window frame - it''s only a minor element, bit the white line it produces could have been avoided.</td>', 'The chair is too tighlty cropped at the top - it is better to show it all than lose only a tiny part of it to the edge. Quite a bright day - the highlights are excessive - there are two points of glare on the seat, and two on the rear. Shooting on a cloudier day, or at a different time of day so the sunlight isn''t so harsh would help. There is a lot of detail in here, but I would have preferred a deeper DoF - the rear table leg also deserves to be in focus.Nice use of the table to provide great leading linse, but they don''t lead to anything! Maybe If you rotated the chair clockwise, so we could see the detail on the front rather than the side, it would help. Another minor distraction is the top of the far char intersecting with the window frame - it''s only a minor element, bit the white line it produces could have been avoided.', '2005-07-25 15:02:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1561855, 208387, 40355, '<td valign="top">Not a bad shot, but it coverest he entire frame and is a little boring</td>', 'Not a bad shot, but it coverest he entire frame and is a little boring', '2005-07-25 15:02:37.000000', NULL, 1),
