(1569548, 208421, 33560, '<td valign="top">Great textures and great color palette.  I love the light and the way the steps curve away into darkness. It strikes me as an inspired choice to place the subject so near the edge of the photo.</td>', 'Great textures and great color palette.  I love the light and the way the steps curve away into darkness. It strikes me as an inspired choice to place the subject so near the edge of the photo.', '2005-07-28 10:53:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569555, 207022, 20941, '<td valign="top">great use of de-sat and composition!</td>', 'great use of de-sat and composition!', '2005-07-28 10:57:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569556, 207607, 20941, '<td valign="top">wonderful angle and composition!</td>', 'wonderful angle and composition!', '2005-07-28 10:57:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569558, 208552, 20941, '<td valign="top">angle, composition and subject excellent!</td>', 'angle, composition and subject excellent!', '2005-07-28 10:58:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569560, 208049, 20941, '<td valign="top">composition and colors are great, focus and lighting coulkd be a little better</td>', 'composition and colors are great, focus and lighting coulkd be a little better', '2005-07-28 10:59:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569561, 208428, 33560, '<td valign="top">There are some wonderful things about this photo.  Technically it is flawless. The stucco and the textures of the two doors and ladder are all quite beautiful.  The items hanging from the ladder are beautiful also.  And the blue folded tarps contrast and balance the aqua door nicely.   The plates on the wall, IMO, ruin a good photo.  They start a new and very different story, one that relates to the hanging food.  And those of us who are easily attracted by food, by stories of food, or even photos of plates depicting food, will find ourselves wandering right out of the picture.  To us, the subject is not in the photo at all.  Sometimes that''s the effect one wants, but I don''t think this is one of them. Still, I like the shot.</td>', 'There are some wonderful things about this photo.  Technically it is flawless. The stucco and the textures of the two doors and ladder are all quite beautiful.  The items hanging from the ladder are beautiful also.  And the blue folded tarps contrast and balance the aqua door nicely.   The plates on the wall, IMO, ruin a good photo.  They start a new and very different story, one that relates to the hanging food.  And those of us who are easily attracted by food, by stories of food, or even photos of plates depicting food, will find ourselves wandering right out of the picture.  To us, the subject is not in the photo at all.  Sometimes that''s the effect one wants, but I don''t think this is one of them. Still, I like the shot.', '2005-07-28 11:01:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569568, 208429, 27482, '<td valign="top">Lovely pattern you caught here, very fitting for this challenge and could have also been in "textures".  Nice shot.</td>', 'Lovely pattern you caught here, very fitting for this challenge and could have also been in "textures".  Nice shot.', '2005-07-28 11:04:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569570, 208551, 20941, '<td valign="top">great subject for this challenge! Lighting conditions look like it made this difficult, in this case I may have chosen to  close in  and meter off one horse to get a clearer shot with more impact.</td>', 'great subject for this challenge! Lighting conditions look like it made this difficult, in this case I may have chosen to  close in  and meter off one horse to get a clearer shot with more impact.', '2005-07-28 11:06:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569571, 207367, 27482, '<td valign="top">I for one would have liked to see the surroundings about this portal, as it is not very interesting as it is right now.  Also I believe this shot would improve if you had used a polarizer to make the sky more dramatic and there is a small dust spot almost in the dead center of the frame.  In short I like this shot but due to all the reasons I just named it´s only an average shot in this challenge for me, 5 from me.</td>', 'I for one would have liked to see the surroundings about this portal, as it is not very interesting as it is right now.  Also I believe this shot would improve if you had used a polarizer to make the sky more dramatic and there is a small dust spot almost in the dead center of the frame.  In short I like this shot but due to all the reasons I just named it´s only an average shot in this challenge for me, 5 from me.', '2005-07-28 11:06:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569576, 208435, 27482, '<td valign="top">Is this Ellidardalur?  I like the composition and although it´s almost too much saturation for my taste the colours are nice and pleasing and this is pretty good.  I don´t think it´s as interesting as it could have been though, there is nothing that makes me wonder about this picture, it´s "merely" pleasing to the eye (wich is good, don´t get me wrong)  Maybe someone standing on the bridge or walking over it would have made it more interesting.  Anyway, one of the better shots in the challenge, hope you do well.</td>', 'Is this Ellidardalur?  I like the composition and although it´s almost too much saturation for my taste the colours are nice and pleasing and this is pretty good.  I don´t think it´s as interesting as it could have been though, there is nothing that makes me wonder about this picture, it´s "merely" pleasing to the eye (wich is good, don´t get me wrong)  Maybe someone standing on the bridge or walking over it would have made it more interesting.  Anyway, one of the better shots in the challenge, hope you do well.', '2005-07-28 11:08:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569578, 207011, 20941, '<td valign="top">This may be a great shot, but its too small to tell ( see tutorials re; resizing) not much to see of anything wooden</td>', 'This may be a great shot, but its too small to tell ( see tutorials re; resizing) not much to see of anything wooden', '2005-07-28 11:10:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569579, 206917, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice, I like the framing, the 2:1 panorama crop works well here.</td>', 'Nice, I like the framing, the 2:1 panorama crop works well here.', '2005-07-28 11:10:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569582, 208554, 20941, '<td valign="top">great composition, use of de-sat and contrast</td>', 'great composition, use of de-sat and contrast', '2005-07-28 11:11:05.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1569584, 206854, 20941, '<td valign="top">cool subject, a bit overexposed</td>', 'cool subject, a bit overexposed', '2005-07-28 11:12:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569586, 207659, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, only thing I want to suggest to make it better is that even though you have the fence at the bottom it´s pretty hard for me to get a sense of scale to this picture and therefore I don´t think it has a strong visual impact as it could have had if you had a person or something that you could relate to more in the shot.  Nice work, I gave it a 7.</td>', 'Nice shot, only thing I want to suggest to make it better is that even though you have the fence at the bottom it´s pretty hard for me to get a sense of scale to this picture and therefore I don´t think it has a strong visual impact as it could have had if you had a person or something that you could relate to more in the shot.  Nice work, I gave it a 7.', '2005-07-28 11:12:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569589, 208624, 27482, '<td valign="top">Clever use of a fisheye, I like the composition.  It looks a bit flat though, maybe some more contrast would improve it?</td>', 'Clever use of a fisheye, I like the composition.  It looks a bit flat though, maybe some more contrast would improve it?', '2005-07-28 11:13:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569591, 208643, 39347, '<td valign="top">Maybe a closer view of the flames and the wood, would have been better. I woould have shot that myself,like a window with flames coming out. The water and firemen are a distraction for me. But a good pic nonetheless.</td>', 'Maybe a closer view of the flames and the wood, would have been better. I woould have shot that myself,like a window with flames coming out. The water and firemen are a distraction for me. But a good pic nonetheless.', '2005-07-28 11:14:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569599, 208407, 33560, '<td valign="top">I like the choice of subject, it''s nicely observed. And the focus on the subject is crisp.<br/> <br/>The problem I see you wrestling with is that this is a challenge about wood, so that ought to be the subject.   Yet the nail has subverted your intentions. It has upstaged the wood, and the wood is the background or it is a supporting cast member.    When faced with this choice, I have tried to err on the side of making a good photo over meeting the challenge.  Most viewers will vote on the quality of the photo  and give some latitude so long as you show you tried to meet the challenge. In this challenge, two of the more memorable of the photos use wood as a secondary element rather than as the primary subject.  <br/> <br/>So... what does al this have to do with this simple photo?  The nail is the subject.  And it is a handsome one.  Somehow, the space around it seems odd.  Since the nail is essentially vertical, we expect the space that frames it to be esssentially vertical.  Or at least it seems to me that much of the space to the right of the nail is wasted.  Similarly, I would wish for a little more space at the bottom of the photo.   On one hand I love the fact that the knot is nicely focussed; on the other, I see how well the out of focus wood frames the nail and I wish more of the wood near the nail were more out of focus.  And I realize you can''t do both.</td>', 'I like the choice of subject, it''s nicely observed. And the focus on the subject is crisp. The problem I see you wrestling with is that this is a challenge about wood, so that ought to be the subject.   Yet the nail has subverted your intentions. It has upstaged the wood, and the wood is the background or it is a supporting cast member.    When faced with this choice, I have tried to err on the side of making a good photo over meeting the challenge.  Most viewers will vote on the quality of the photo  and give some latitude so long as you show you tried to meet the challenge. In this challenge, two of the more memorable of the photos use wood as a secondary element rather than as the primary subject.   So... what does al this have to do with this simple photo?  The nail is the subject.  And it is a handsome one.  Somehow, the space around it seems odd.  Since the nail is essentially vertical, we expect the space that frames it to be esssentially vertical.  Or at least it seems to me that much of the space to the right of the nail is wasted.  Similarly, I would wish for a little more space at the bottom of the photo.   On one hand I love the fact that the knot is nicely focussed; on the other, I see how well the out of focus wood frames the nail and I wish more of the wood near the nail were more out of focus.  And I realize you can''t do both.', '2005-07-28 11:16:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569602, 208676, 33560, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.  It was an inspired choice to give us a clue in blurry form what it is we are looking at.</td>', 'Beautiful.  It was an inspired choice to give us a clue in blurry form what it is we are looking at.', '2005-07-28 11:18:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569605, 207849, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice, good choice to make this sepia toned and I like the composition and the fact that it tilts down to the right.  However, I don´t think it´s sharp enough, did something happen when you downsized it or is it just out of focus or did you forget to sharpen it after resizing it?  <br/> <br/>Ááááfram Ísland.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Nice, good choice to make this sepia toned and I like the composition and the fact that it tilts down to the right.  However, I don´t think it´s sharp enough, did something happen when you downsized it or is it just out of focus or did you forget to sharpen it after resizing it?   Ááááfram Ísland. ', '2005-07-28 11:18:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569608, 207830, 33560, '<td valign="top">A lovely shot of a very attractive door.  It''s skillfully framed, nicely  lit, perfectly exposed.</td>', 'A lovely shot of a very attractive door.  It''s skillfully framed, nicely  lit, perfectly exposed.', '2005-07-28 11:19:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569623, 206345, 39347, '<td valign="top">The bench almost looks cartoonish.</td>', 'The bench almost looks cartoonish.', '2005-07-28 11:22:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569625, 208492, 20941, '<td valign="top">wonderful composition and subject that makes you think about the story behind this image. very cool</td>', 'wonderful composition and subject that makes you think about the story behind this image. very cool', '2005-07-28 11:23:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569629, 208180, 20941, '<td valign="top">focus seems to have suffered a bit in difficult lighting conditions</td>', 'focus seems to have suffered a bit in difficult lighting conditions', '2005-07-28 11:24:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569638, 208635, 34194, '<td valign="top">Decent shot but boat is too centered. Details seem pixelated.</td>', 'Decent shot but boat is too centered. Details seem pixelated.', '2005-07-28 11:26:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569644, 208609, 33560, '<td valign="top">Nice use of a mirror.  The subject is beautifully lit, framed, and photographed.  The weedy backdrop, gratefully, has been cropped right and bottom.  And the darkness of the grotto makes the frame stand out well.    The left side ot the photo seems too tangled and full of distracting detail to quite work.  One wonders whether this photo would not work better taken in fading, cloudy or misty daylight where the shadows are very gentle.  Then the lighting might have been managed to de-emphasize the tangle of weeds near the left margin.  Perhaps lower light would also allow DOF manipulation more favorable to this goal.</td>', 'Nice use of a mirror.  The subject is beautifully lit, framed, and photographed.  The weedy backdrop, gratefully, has been cropped right and bottom.  And the darkness of the grotto makes the frame stand out well.    The left side ot the photo seems too tangled and full of distracting detail to quite work.  One wonders whether this photo would not work better taken in fading, cloudy or misty daylight where the shadows are very gentle.  Then the lighting might have been managed to de-emphasize the tangle of weeds near the left margin.  Perhaps lower light would also allow DOF manipulation more favorable to this goal.', '2005-07-28 11:27:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569652, 208387, 33560, '<td valign="top">I love this simple presentation.  Were the challenge something other than ''wood,''  I suppose I would assert that the blankness of the left side overbalances the more interesting right.</td>', 'I love this simple presentation.  Were the challenge something other than ''wood,''  I suppose I would assert that the blankness of the left side overbalances the more interesting right.', '2005-07-28 11:29:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1569654, 207619, 34194, '<td valign="top">I''m sure you have tons of comments on this shot. Very cool, I hope you will write a tutorial on how this is done.</td>', 'I''m sure you have tons of comments on this shot. Very cool, I hope you will write a tutorial on how this is done.', '2005-07-28 11:30:50.000000', NULL, 1),
