(1571754, 208375, 37334, '<td valign="top">What a gorgeous image - the colours make me feel so calm as does the softness.9</td>', 'What a gorgeous image - the colours make me feel so calm as does the softness.9', '2005-07-29 11:40:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571757, 208463, 37334, '<td valign="top">Nice lighting and colour.</td>', 'Nice lighting and colour.', '2005-07-29 11:42:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571760, 207046, 37334, '<td valign="top">There is something so appealing and evocative about his image. The angle is quirky but shows off the wood texure well. I want to know more about the woman;)</td>', 'There is something so appealing and evocative about his image. The angle is quirky but shows off the wood texure well. I want to know more about the woman;)', '2005-07-29 11:44:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571770, 207828, 27482, '<td valign="top">Not a bad take on the challenge, I like the composition but the image seems a bit flat, maybe some more contrast would improve it?</td>', 'Not a bad take on the challenge, I like the composition but the image seems a bit flat, maybe some more contrast would improve it?', '2005-07-29 11:54:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571771, 208446, 27482, '<td valign="top">Very nice, I like the simplicity in this shot and the odd repeating pattern.  Exposure is spot on.</td>', 'Very nice, I like the simplicity in this shot and the odd repeating pattern.  Exposure is spot on.', '2005-07-29 11:55:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571773, 208560, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice, LOVE the dof and image quality but the selective desaturation is hurting the image instead of helping it IMHO.  Still one of the very best in the challenge as far as I am concerned!  8 from me.</td>', 'Nice, LOVE the dof and image quality but the selective desaturation is hurting the image instead of helping it IMHO.  Still one of the very best in the challenge as far as I am concerned!  8 from me.', '2005-07-29 11:56:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571835, 207011, 31403, '<td valign="top">I don''t see any wood, beautiful photo though</td>', 'I don''t see any wood, beautiful photo though', '2005-07-29 12:48:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571838, 208519, 20667, '<td valign="top">Would this have looked better in the landscape format? I wonder...Nice shot.</td>', 'Would this have looked better in the landscape format? I wonder...Nice shot.', '2005-07-29 12:49:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571839, 208549, 31403, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure what this is a photo of.  If it''s the fence, it needs to be cropped closer, the barn?  way too far out of frame for that, the clouds, the horizon line is too high.  The tones here are really nice, just a touch more contrast for my taste, but the composition leaves me scratching my head -  4</td>', 'I''m not sure what this is a photo of.  If it''s the fence, it needs to be cropped closer, the barn?  way too far out of frame for that, the clouds, the horizon line is too high.  The tones here are really nice, just a touch more contrast for my taste, but the composition leaves me scratching my head -  4', '2005-07-29 12:50:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571843, 207844, 31403, '<td valign="top">lighting feels too harsh, the hard lined shadows give me this feeling along with the very strong highlights.  Great title,</td>', 'lighting feels too harsh, the hard lined shadows give me this feeling along with the very strong highlights.  Great title,', '2005-07-29 12:52:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571846, 208686, 20667, '<td valign="top">When I see this photo, I realize that you are trying to use the diagonal lines for composition. But it doesnt seem to be doing anything for the photo. Also, something is happening with magenta colour of the bark and the really colourful background (though it is out of focus).<br/>I think this photo could use some sharpening. It might look better in b&amp;w. I wonder how diffeternt it would have been if you had tried to make the hole formed by the bark (upper left corner of this photo) as the center.<br/>These are my thoughts, as all.</td>', 'When I see this photo, I realize that you are trying to use the diagonal lines for composition. But it doesnt seem to be doing anything for the photo. Also, something is happening with magenta colour of the bark and the really colourful background (though it is out of focus).I think this photo could use some sharpening. It might look better in b&w. I wonder how diffeternt it would have been if you had tried to make the hole formed by the bark (upper left corner of this photo) as the center.These are my thoughts, as all.', '2005-07-29 12:55:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571849, 207800, 31403, '<td valign="top">very flat, harsh light - the on-board flash? - makes this look like a snapshot.  Tough subject to shoot in interesting ways, maybe set up a table in front and use this for a background?  So between the tough subject and the flood light source, I''ve given you my standard "snapshot" score of 3.  Hope that helps.</td>', 'very flat, harsh light - the on-board flash? - makes this look like a snapshot.  Tough subject to shoot in interesting ways, maybe set up a table in front and use this for a background?  So between the tough subject and the flood light source, I''ve given you my standard "snapshot" score of 3.  Hope that helps.', '2005-07-29 12:56:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571853, 206665, 31403, '<td valign="top">not sure why you are sorry, or why he''s sorry, but great tones, love this!  8 for now, but I''ll be back to bump it up</td>', 'not sure why you are sorry, or why he''s sorry, but great tones, love this!  8 for now, but I''ll be back to bump it up', '2005-07-29 12:57:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571857, 207060, 20667, '<td valign="top">Nice horse. I think this photo is just a little overexposed. A bit of sharpness and contrast can be desired. Shooting this in the evening would also help. I''m guessing this photo was taken during midday. The overblown sky and the extra trees in the background aren''t doing anything for the photograph. I would suggest trying to crop it out. Also, moving a bit to the left so that there is space in front of the horse, rather than behind it would have been nice.</td>', 'Nice horse. I think this photo is just a little overexposed. A bit of sharpness and contrast can be desired. Shooting this in the evening would also help. I''m guessing this photo was taken during midday. The overblown sky and the extra trees in the background aren''t doing anything for the photograph. I would suggest trying to crop it out. Also, moving a bit to the left so that there is space in front of the horse, rather than behind it would have been nice.', '2005-07-29 12:59:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571859, 208683, 31403, '<td valign="top">my eye wants to see the cat lower and further left by half a cat - but that may just make it different, not better.  REALLY cool concept - great overall color scheme for me, I really like this.  Aren''t you glad you didn''t seal that deck yet?  the weathered wood is really nice.  Maybe some dodge and burn to accent that more?  there''s my two cents, and it might be overpriced at that!  :)  great work - 7 for now, will revisit</td>', 'my eye wants to see the cat lower and further left by half a cat - but that may just make it different, not better.  REALLY cool concept - great overall color scheme for me, I really like this.  Aren''t you glad you didn''t seal that deck yet?  the weathered wood is really nice.  Maybe some dodge and burn to accent that more?  there''s my two cents, and it might be overpriced at that!  :)  great work - 7 for now, will revisit', '2005-07-29 13:00:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1571861, 208666, 20667, '<td valign="top">Would straightening the nonexistent horizon help in any way?<br/>Nice shot.</td>', 'Would straightening the nonexistent horizon help in any way?Nice shot.', '2005-07-29 13:01:22.000000', NULL, 1),
