(1591293, 208088, 6349, '<td valign="top">beautiful image.  should have placed much higher.</td>', 'beautiful image.  should have placed much higher.', '2005-08-06 20:09:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591429, 206854, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Composition is nicely executed, but saturation might have been bumped up a bit too much as this looks over-processed and the sky totally blown out. I like the soft focus which gives it the dreamy feel. Not all bad for a "dinky little camera"<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** Composition is nicely executed, but saturation might have been bumped up a bit too much as this looks over-processed and the sky totally blown out. I like the soft focus which gives it the dreamy feel. Not all bad for a "dinky little camera" - Linda', '2005-08-06 22:16:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591440, 207174, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Good DOF. A little soft on focus. Color balance is right on. There are two distractions here - the orange lighting appearing through the gap in the boards, and whatever the brown thing is that is sticking up between two other boards. <br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** Good DOF. A little soft on focus. Color balance is right on. There are two distractions here - the orange lighting appearing through the gap in the boards, and whatever the brown thing is that is sticking up between two other boards.  - Linda', '2005-08-06 22:23:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591483, 207379, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Very moving entry for the wooden challenge. It send a strong message in my opinion. I would have like to see more of the lower end of the cross, but even as is the photo is very nice. The colors are all very complimentary.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** Very moving entry for the wooden challenge. It send a strong message in my opinion. I would have like to see more of the lower end of the cross, but even as is the photo is very nice. The colors are all very complimentary. - Linda', '2005-08-06 22:48:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591488, 208278, 19353, '<td valign="top">Some commentors didn''t care for the greenish tint to the water. Normally, I might agree, but in this case, I thought the green water played better (and offered more contrast) against the blues and golds of the boat. Nice job.</td>', 'Some commentors didn''t care for the greenish tint to the water. Normally, I might agree, but in this case, I thought the green water played better (and offered more contrast) against the blues and golds of the boat. Nice job.', '2005-08-06 22:53:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591489, 208518, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>What a beautiful piece of work. Excellent use of filter and post-processing skills. I love the textures that are displayed in such awesome detail. Colors are right on too. My only suggestion would be to include more of the foreground, off to the right or left to give a feeling that one was being led to the shack.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** What a beautiful piece of work. Excellent use of filter and post-processing skills. I love the textures that are displayed in such awesome detail. Colors are right on too. My only suggestion would be to include more of the foreground, off to the right or left to give a feeling that one was being led to the shack. - Linda', '2005-08-06 22:54:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591496, 208499, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Kinda cool - but would have liked to see more of the tree as a whole as you mentioned it is sitting on the edge of a cliff - would have added interest to it. The flash really hurts this image, as the artificial light really blows out the highlights of the wood.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** Kinda cool - but would have liked to see more of the tree as a whole as you mentioned it is sitting on the edge of a cliff - would have added interest to it. The flash really hurts this image, as the artificial light really blows out the highlights of the wood. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:01:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591502, 208644, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Composition: Would have liked to see this not centered so much, and a little less foreground.<br/>Technically: The sky does not look natural in color - perhaps you adjusted the color range a little too much? It really looks odd against the green of the trees leaves. The greens are nice. Best bet would have been to convert thisto black and white, or sepia tones.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** Composition: Would have liked to see this not centered so much, and a little less foreground.Technically: The sky does not look natural in color - perhaps you adjusted the color range a little too much? It really looks odd against the green of the trees leaves. The greens are nice. Best bet would have been to convert thisto black and white, or sepia tones. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:05:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591506, 208600, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>To me, the focus looks too soft. Composition is weak - perhaps if you had taken this at an angle and increased the DOF it would have brought mroe interest to the photo. There seems to be a lot fo noise in the image also.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** To me, the focus looks too soft. Composition is weak - perhaps if you had taken this at an angle and increased the DOF it would have brought mroe interest to the photo. There seems to be a lot fo noise in the image also. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:08:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591516, 207791, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>What a cool old bridge. Would have been nice to see the inside timbers better - maybe more fill flash or curves adjustment in post-processing would have helped.  I like the feeling of being led across the bridge. The colors on the other side of the bridge are nice, but could use a little pop.<br/> <br/>- Linda<br/></td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** What a cool old bridge. Would have been nice to see the inside timbers better - maybe more fill flash or curves adjustment in post-processing would have helped.  I like the feeling of being led across the bridge. The colors on the other side of the bridge are nice, but could use a little pop. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:14:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591519, 208439, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>I love this photo - but the frame is much too heavy. Not sure black was a good color choice for the frame either.  A rich brown frame - much thinner comes to mind as a better choice.<br/>Colors within the photo are beautiful. Great DOF and focus. Excellent composition.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** I love this photo - but the frame is much too heavy. Not sure black was a good color choice for the frame either.  A rich brown frame - much thinner comes to mind as a better choice.Colors within the photo are beautiful. Great DOF and focus. Excellent composition. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:17:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591529, 208439, 31399, '<td valign="top">thanks Linda...and shoot me next time I try something new...never entered my mind to put NO frame..lol...I did debate between this one entered and one with white border and small brown border inside white border..but i thought the wide black made it look more 3d or something..i dunno WHAT i''z thinking..lol<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-06 22:23:50.</i></td>', 'thanks Linda...and shoot me next time I try something new...never entered my mind to put NO frame..lol...I did debate between this one entered and one with white border and small brown border inside white border..but i thought the wide black made it look more 3d or something..i dunno WHAT i''z thinking..lol', '2005-08-06 23:22:20.000000', '2005-08-06 23:23:50.000000', 0),
(1591545, 208590, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Simple yet nicely executed. The top edge of the spoon seems a little soft focused, but the rest of the image has nice detail. The lower corners of this image have a blue cast - not sure what caused that but it is a bit odd.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club ** Simple yet nicely executed. The top edge of the spoon seems a little soft focused, but the rest of the image has nice detail. The lower corners of this image have a blue cast - not sure what caused that but it is a bit odd. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:40:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591552, 207369, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>What an emotionally strong photo! I love the selective desat work you have applied. DOF and detail are wonderful. The purpels really pop and add a lot to this image.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  What an emotionally strong photo! I love the selective desat work you have applied. DOF and detail are wonderful. The purpels really pop and add a lot to this image. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:46:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591553, 206668, 37673, '<td valign="top">Very nice picture.  A couple of distractions but no big deal.  What ever is in the fore ground could be cropped a little. The power poles are a little distracting. The subject needed to be a little clearer in the detail to confirm it is wood but that too is minor. Color and contrast or good considering you didn''t use all the meg pixels available.  Over all I really do like the picture. It is very nicely done.  Would look wonderful in a frame on a wall near a window.  Congrats, nicely done<br/></td>', 'Very nice picture.  A couple of distractions but no big deal.  What ever is in the fore ground could be cropped a little. The power poles are a little distracting. The subject needed to be a little clearer in the detail to confirm it is wood but that too is minor. Color and contrast or good considering you didn''t use all the meg pixels available.  Over all I really do like the picture. It is very nicely done.  Would look wonderful in a frame on a wall near a window.  Congrats, nicely done', '2005-08-06 23:46:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591556, 208597, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Composition: strong and well executed<br/>Technically: Appears over sharpened as if it were done to attmept correction of the poor focus. Good use of B&amp;W<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Composition: strong and well executedTechnically: Appears over sharpened as if it were done to attmept correction of the poor focus. Good use of B&W - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:48:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591570, 208679, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>At first glance this is a very grabbing image. But as you keep looking, the specks on the water become distracting from the beauty of the reflection. I love the composition and lines. As for the over-saturation, I am not a fan of this and even here I think you have pushed the limits a bit too much.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  At first glance this is a very grabbing image. But as you keep looking, the specks on the water become distracting from the beauty of the reflection. I love the composition and lines. As for the over-saturation, I am not a fan of this and even here I think you have pushed the limits a bit too much. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:53:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591582, 208414, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>An excellent use of natural light. The softness of the light works well with the soft focus applied here. It was a little hard to pick up on the water at first though. <br/> <br/>Congrats on your top 10 finish.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  An excellent use of natural light. The softness of the light works well with the soft focus applied here. It was a little hard to pick up on the water at first though.  Congrats on your top 10 finish. - Linda', '2005-08-06 23:58:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591585, 208662, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>The lack of focus, and detail really impairs this image. The colors also appear washed out across the horizon. You must have had to use a high ISO as there is a bit of noise througout the sky. A fill flash might have been nice to bring out colors in the grass.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  The lack of focus, and detail really impairs this image. The colors also appear washed out across the horizon. You must have had to use a high ISO as there is a bit of noise througout the sky. A fill flash might have been nice to bring out colors in the grass. - Linda', '2005-08-07 00:02:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591726, 208630, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>A really fun shot! The composition is excellent. You did a very good job of keeping the exposure settings under control, preventing any blown out areas. The sky - due to time of day most likely - could use a bit more color. Perhaps with an adjustment in color balance or saturation this would have given the sky more depth and blue tone - which in turn would have added pop to the rest of the image. <br/>Your timing was great - good choice of shuuter spped!<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  A really fun shot! The composition is excellent. You did a very good job of keeping the exposure settings under control, preventing any blown out areas. The sky - due to time of day most likely - could use a bit more color. Perhaps with an adjustment in color balance or saturation this would have given the sky more depth and blue tone - which in turn would have added pop to the rest of the image. Your timing was great - good choice of shuuter spped! - Linda', '2005-08-07 01:09:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591756, 207817, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Good DOF and focus on the bird and his perch, but the fence is awkward. I must say, you did well in at least blurring it and playing the light off it. The color balance is right on here. I also like the framing on this. <br/>As for keeping within the realm of the challenge - I do think this was a bit of a stretch as the subject seems to be more the bird than the wooden perch.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Good DOF and focus on the bird and his perch, but the fence is awkward. I must say, you did well in at least blurring it and playing the light off it. The color balance is right on here. I also like the framing on this. As for keeping within the realm of the challenge - I do think this was a bit of a stretch as the subject seems to be more the bird than the wooden perch. - Linda', '2005-08-07 01:29:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591766, 207130, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Very interesting image. The colors are vibrant. DOF is good. Focus is soft - but is well suited for this image. Interesting that you entered this in the wooden challenge though as the subject does not strike me to be the pruple painted wood, but the algae filled stream itself.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Very interesting image. The colors are vibrant. DOF is good. Focus is soft - but is well suited for this image. Interesting that you entered this in the wooden challenge though as the subject does not strike me to be the pruple painted wood, but the algae filled stream itself. - Linda', '2005-08-07 01:36:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591773, 208212, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Very simplistic - but appealing. I really like the creativity. The focus on the clothes pins seems a little soft. The spacing of the pins is good - but perhaps shooting from a slight angle would have made this even more interesting.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Very simplistic - but appealing. I really like the creativity. The focus on the clothes pins seems a little soft. The spacing of the pins is good - but perhaps shooting from a slight angle would have made this even more interesting. - Linda', '2005-08-07 01:39:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591780, 208677, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>A very creative image for this challenge. I like your thinking. <br/>A couple suggestions - use of a white china cup possibly would have added some nice contrast. Possibly increase the DOF - the background is a bit too blurred out in my opinion. The cropping and frame work well here.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  A very creative image for this challenge. I like your thinking. A couple suggestions - use of a white china cup possibly would have added some nice contrast. Possibly increase the DOF - the background is a bit too blurred out in my opinion. The cropping and frame work well here. - Linda', '2005-08-07 01:43:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591862, 207801, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Unique entry - does not really grab attention though as the subject is not clearly defined. I think this would fair better if not so close up. Might also suggest an increased DOF.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Unique entry - does not really grab attention though as the subject is not clearly defined. I think this would fair better if not so close up. Might also suggest an increased DOF. - Linda', '2005-08-07 02:47:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591867, 207254, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Although the image is a bit darker than what I usually like - the lighting and shadows reflect beautiful textures of the wood. The breass ring breaks up the darkness, adding the perfect contrast. The green rug is a big minus here - it clashes rather than enhances. I would suggest some hue manipulation to better blend it into the same color scheme of the brass ring and wood.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Although the image is a bit darker than what I usually like - the lighting and shadows reflect beautiful textures of the wood. The breass ring breaks up the darkness, adding the perfect contrast. The green rug is a big minus here - it clashes rather than enhances. I would suggest some hue manipulation to better blend it into the same color scheme of the brass ring and wood. - Linda', '2005-08-07 02:51:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591870, 207643, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>I absolutely ,loved this when I first saw it, and still do. The 3D effect it presents is great.  The vibrant colors just pop out at me. I can''t help but smile when viewing this.<br/>Great shot - shows some welcome creativity.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  I absolutely ,loved this when I first saw it, and still do. The 3D effect it presents is great.  The vibrant colors just pop out at me. I can''t help but smile when viewing this.Great shot - shows some welcome creativity. - Linda', '2005-08-07 02:55:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591894, 208519, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Somehow fire / flames never stop intriguing us. Good shot here, although I feel the crop is a bit tight. Good exposure level as the textures of the burning wood center of the pit are well demonstrated.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Somehow fire / flames never stop intriguing us. Good shot here, although I feel the crop is a bit tight. Good exposure level as the textures of the burning wood center of the pit are well demonstrated. - Linda', '2005-08-07 03:12:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591902, 206859, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>The image seems much too dark imho. Use of a fill flash, or proper metering would have prevented the staute from being backlight and given it a more appealing look. The textures of the wood are hidden in the shadows. The DOF, focus, or both were just not working for you here as all appears too blurry. As for the trees in the background - too distracting. By moving more to the left perhaps you could have gotten the statue alone against the blue sky.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  The image seems much too dark imho. Use of a fill flash, or proper metering would have prevented the staute from being backlight and given it a more appealing look. The textures of the wood are hidden in the shadows. The DOF, focus, or both were just not working for you here as all appears too blurry. As for the trees in the background - too distracting. By moving more to the left perhaps you could have gotten the statue alone against the blue sky. - Linda', '2005-08-07 03:17:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591919, 208659, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>A very creative image, and nice too see in this challenge. The colors are vibrant, and the lighting pretty good - other than the glare off the right side of the moon. Perhaps just by positioning your light differently, bouncing it, or post-processing this could have been corrected. I really like the composition.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  A very creative image, and nice too see in this challenge. The colors are vibrant, and the lighting pretty good - other than the glare off the right side of the moon. Perhaps just by positioning your light differently, bouncing it, or post-processing this could have been corrected. I really like the composition. - Linda', '2005-08-07 03:34:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591921, 207754, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Cropped a bit tightly, and a little too dark in my opinion. I like the way the light was casted upon the ladder, but the sun spots are a bit much.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Cropped a bit tightly, and a little too dark in my opinion. I like the way the light was casted upon the ladder, but the sun spots are a bit much. - Linda', '2005-08-07 03:37:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591928, 207290, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Another masterpiece! I love the creativity here, and the cleverness to pull it off. There really is not much to say but EXCELLENT - the contast, texture, DOF, focus, all so perfect!<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Another masterpiece! I love the creativity here, and the cleverness to pull it off. There really is not much to say but EXCELLENT - the contast, texture, DOF, focus, all so perfect! - Linda', '2005-08-07 03:44:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591932, 206144, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>A unique and refreshing take on the challenge. A whimsical photo with appeal. The placement of the chairs - their angles against the angle of the wood floor planks - really was just right. Seems just a bit grainy, but being that this is wood it does not distract from the photo in my opinion.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  A unique and refreshing take on the challenge. A whimsical photo with appeal. The placement of the chairs - their angles against the angle of the wood floor planks - really was just right. Seems just a bit grainy, but being that this is wood it does not distract from the photo in my opinion. - Linda', '2005-08-07 03:49:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591942, 208520, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Simple, but effective. The wood texture really comes out on this image as a result of good exposure control. Composition is good also. The leaf adds a nice tough - wish it were a bit more in focus though. DOF is nice.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Simple, but effective. The wood texture really comes out on this image as a result of good exposure control. Composition is good also. The leaf adds a nice tough - wish it were a bit more in focus though. DOF is nice. - Linda', '2005-08-07 03:58:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591944, 208149, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>A cute photo of an adorable little boy - yet misses the mark as far as making wood a major element. The boy and the brightness of the sky showing through trees is what catches my eye first most - the wood is simply a small element that the child is posed upon. As far as technical eval: the DOF is perfect in my opinion. I would have tried to tone down the brightness of the sky, and not cropped the top so closely (unless of course it would have brought more of the bright sky into play)Focus is nice and sharp. Colors are right on.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  A cute photo of an adorable little boy - yet misses the mark as far as making wood a major element. The boy and the brightness of the sky showing through trees is what catches my eye first most - the wood is simply a small element that the child is posed upon. As far as technical eval: the DOF is perfect in my opinion. I would have tried to tone down the brightness of the sky, and not cropped the top so closely (unless of course it would have brought more of the bright sky into play)Focus is nice and sharp. Colors are right on. - Linda', '2005-08-07 04:04:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591947, 208387, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Good DOF and Focus. Lighting works well here. The subject matter is not very interesting, but the contrasting lines and angles give a plus to this image. Unique.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Good DOF and Focus. Lighting works well here. The subject matter is not very interesting, but the contrasting lines and angles give a plus to this image. Unique. - Linda', '2005-08-07 04:08:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591955, 208638, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>Colors work very well together here, however there seems to be a gradient lighting. Looks as if the on-board flash was used, creating a glare on some of the foremost wood, and fading to dark along the top. Perhaps having the lighting come from the side, raking across the textures of this chair would have created an entirely different and interesting mood. Focus is sharp.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  Colors work very well together here, however there seems to be a gradient lighting. Looks as if the on-board flash was used, creating a glare on some of the foremost wood, and fading to dark along the top. Perhaps having the lighting come from the side, raking across the textures of this chair would have created an entirely different and interesting mood. Focus is sharp. - Linda', '2005-08-07 04:13:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591958, 208543, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>The DOF given this scene is wonderful. I equally like the colors, focus, and leading lines. The people seem to be a distraction imho. As for meeting the challenge - keeping wood as the main subject, I don''t see it here.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  The DOF given this scene is wonderful. I equally like the colors, focus, and leading lines. The people seem to be a distraction imho. As for meeting the challenge - keeping wood as the main subject, I don''t see it here. - Linda', '2005-08-07 04:18:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591972, 205728, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>What a cute simplistic image. I love the little wooden buckets - and yes I can see by the construction of the handles on them they are indeed wooden. The lighting is cast in such a manner that it gradually fades out but not too harshly. I like that. The only objection I have is the cropping. The missing handle on the first bucket is a distracting feature.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  What a cute simplistic image. I love the little wooden buckets - and yes I can see by the construction of the handles on them they are indeed wooden. The lighting is cast in such a manner that it gradually fades out but not too harshly. I like that. The only objection I have is the cropping. The missing handle on the first bucket is a distracting feature. - Linda', '2005-08-07 04:25:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591979, 208300, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>An interesting entry to the challenge. The composition is good, yet I tend to think maybe a bit more off the top would have been better. The dual tonality is very nice - really sets the image out there. Lighting was perfect.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  An interesting entry to the challenge. The composition is good, yet I tend to think maybe a bit more off the top would have been better. The dual tonality is very nice - really sets the image out there. Lighting was perfect. - Linda', '2005-08-07 04:32:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1591987, 208597, 23318, '<td valign="top">This is one of my fav. subjects, and have stopped there 3 or 4 times since finding it origionally. It''s interesting to watch it deteriorate in the images that I have of it, and yours (haven''t been there in 6 - 8 months or so)<br/> <br/>This is a great image of it, and knowing exactly where you were standing makes me wonder if I should have stood there last time I was there. I think your over sharpened comments may be from a larger than normal amount of contrast, which makes it look over sharpened a bit. Your ISO being higher than what I normally shoot, makes it difficult for me to be sure. Great image, and hopefully you and i stay off the same subjects for future challenges, as I almost went back out there and reshot for this particular challenge. <br/> <br/></td>', 'This is one of my fav. subjects, and have stopped there 3 or 4 times since finding it origionally. It''s interesting to watch it deteriorate in the images that I have of it, and yours (haven''t been there in 6 - 8 months or so) This is a great image of it, and knowing exactly where you were standing makes me wonder if I should have stood there last time I was there. I think your over sharpened comments may be from a larger than normal amount of contrast, which makes it look over sharpened a bit. Your ISO being higher than what I normally shoot, makes it difficult for me to be sure. Great image, and hopefully you and i stay off the same subjects for future challenges, as I almost went back out there and reshot for this particular challenge.  ', '2005-08-07 04:36:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1592005, 208683, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>An interesting entry. The kitty really gives meaning to an otherwise plain image. The DOF is good, but the angle makes it hard to discern where the one step ends and the second begins along the right side. The cat is perhaps the only thing that truly discerns this on the left.<br/>The boards along the top of the image seem a bit too bright - perhaps from the time of day this was shot? Focus seems a little soft.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  An interesting entry. The kitty really gives meaning to an otherwise plain image. The DOF is good, but the angle makes it hard to discern where the one step ends and the second begins along the right side. The cat is perhaps the only thing that truly discerns this on the left.The boards along the top of the image seem a bit too bright - perhaps from the time of day this was shot? Focus seems a little soft. - Linda', '2005-08-07 04:59:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1592010, 208520, 16241, '<td valign="top">i like it!  keep going in this direction........ :))</td>', 'i like it!  keep going in this direction........ :))', '2005-08-07 05:10:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1592015, 208633, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>An interesting look at the broken heart of an old chair. DOF is perhaps a bit too shallow as the wood just above the heart would be better in focus. Color saturation is very good. Slight glare along the edge of the heart but doesn''t take away from the image at all. <br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  An interesting look at the broken heart of an old chair. DOF is perhaps a bit too shallow as the wood just above the heart would be better in focus. Color saturation is very good. Slight glare along the edge of the heart but doesn''t take away from the image at all.  - Linda', '2005-08-07 05:27:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1592017, 207597, 37252, '<td valign="top">** Greetings from the Critique Club ** <br/> <br/>A bit soft in focus. In this case, a wider DOF might have worked better, at least to the extent of keeping all the digit of the clcok in focus. Lighting seems very good. Cropped / composed well.<br/> <br/>- Linda</td>', '** Greetings from the Critique Club **  A bit soft in focus. In this case, a wider DOF might have worked better, at least to the extent of keeping all the digit of the clcok in focus. Lighting seems very good. Cropped / composed well. - Linda', '2005-08-07 05:31:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1592308, 207290, 19936, '<td valign="top">Make him stop!  Damn this kid is good.  Heaven help us with the new camera coming.</td>', 'Make him stop!  Damn this kid is good.  Heaven help us with the new camera coming.', '2005-08-07 13:12:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1592846, 207918, 19303, '<td valign="top">It''s too noisy.</td>', 'It''s too noisy.', '2005-08-07 21:13:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1594813, 206210, 30049, '<td valign="top">Now that looks like fun.  ;^)<br/> <br/>This is a decent shot - the time of day (lighting) makes it a bit challenging as some of the whites are a little overexposed.  Where did you set the focus/metering?  The white on the front of the canoe would have been a good steady spot to get the metering correct and with enough DOF would not have impacted the focus for the rest of the people, etc...<br/> <br/>What got lost in the crop?  If you cropped water from the lower section that''s probably best - could have left a bit more trees in if they were there.<br/> <br/>Anyhow...good job overall.  Keep smiling and having fun!<br/>Barry</td>', 'Now that looks like fun.  ;^) This is a decent shot - the time of day (lighting) makes it a bit challenging as some of the whites are a little overexposed.  Where did you set the focus/metering?  The white on the front of the canoe would have been a good steady spot to get the metering correct and with enough DOF would not have impacted the focus for the rest of the people, etc... What got lost in the crop?  If you cropped water from the lower section that''s probably best - could have left a bit more trees in if they were there. Anyhow...good job overall.  Keep smiling and having fun!Barry', '2005-08-08 12:34:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1596192, 206345, 39375, '<td valign="top">i LOVED this shot....gave it a 10!</td>', 'i LOVED this shot....gave it a 10!', '2005-08-08 21:47:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1596566, 208619, 31727, '<td valign="top">Heid,I really like your photos.Tell me is easy to get around In Ice Land?You just keep on shooting.</td>', 'Heid,I really like your photos.Tell me is easy to get around In Ice Land?You just keep on shooting.', '2005-08-08 23:22:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1597496, 208275, 30049, '<td valign="top">This was a pretty cool idea.  Interesting use of lighting.  The shadow is fine - actually wish I could see all of it.  Did you try rotating the shot or image to have the wood object and shadow fall diagonally across the image?  Anyhow...have fun, keep smiling!</td>', 'This was a pretty cool idea.  Interesting use of lighting.  The shadow is fine - actually wish I could see all of it.  Did you try rotating the shot or image to have the wood object and shadow fall diagonally across the image?  Anyhow...have fun, keep smiling!', '2005-08-09 10:38:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1598495, 208492, 40526, '<td valign="top">very good.</td>', 'very good.', '2005-08-09 19:03:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1598538, 208634, 25655, '<td valign="top">oh wow... didn''t see that during the challenge!<br/>I think it''s great! the texture is perfect, the light and shadows work well for me. those vertical lines and their horizontal complementary...<br/>I think it''s completely underrated! Should have been way way higher.</td>', 'oh wow... didn''t see that during the challenge!I think it''s great! the texture is perfect, the light and shadows work well for me. those vertical lines and their horizontal complementary...I think it''s completely underrated! Should have been way way higher.', '2005-08-09 19:39:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1598558, 208387, 37719, '<td valign="top">Thought this was a clear image with very nice contrasting textures with the wood overall the strongest.  The rest I thought only served to make the wood stand out - the branches almost acting as leading lines.  Nice clarity and focus, good control of the natural light.</td>', 'Thought this was a clear image with very nice contrasting textures with the wood overall the strongest.  The rest I thought only served to make the wood stand out - the branches almost acting as leading lines.  Nice clarity and focus, good control of the natural light.', '2005-08-09 20:02:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1599931, 208634, 32602, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments. I''m not sure whether I like this pic or not. It looked better before resizing and uploading. I was glad to just get up, get out and take a photo at the time.<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments. I''m not sure whether I like this pic or not. It looked better before resizing and uploading. I was glad to just get up, get out and take a photo at the time.', '2005-08-10 03:31:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1602751, 208033, 41802, '<td valign="top">This is great.  I <b> love</b> the shot!!   Hey where did you get your Woodie?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-10 22:34:25.</i></td>', 'This is great.  I  love the shot!!   Hey where did you get your Woodie?', '2005-08-10 23:33:44.000000', '2005-08-10 23:34:25.000000', 0),
(1602767, 207583, 41802, '<td valign="top">This is cute.  I also like the background.  Where did you pick up your Woodie? I am just curious, I haven''t seen them around.</td>', 'This is cute.  I also like the background.  Where did you pick up your Woodie? I am just curious, I haven''t seen them around.', '2005-08-10 23:40:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1605154, 207738, 41476, '<td valign="top">this is a very pretty photo with crisp colours</td>', 'this is a very pretty photo with crisp colours', '2005-08-12 00:11:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1608798, 207936, 34659, '<td valign="top">I remember this one from the challenge - great capture!  How long did you sit out there to get this shot?!?  ;-)  Perfect crop, great colors, &amp; good DOF.  Nice job!</td>', 'I remember this one from the challenge - great capture!  How long did you sit out there to get this shot?!?  ;-)  Perfect crop, great colors, & good DOF.  Nice job!', '2005-08-13 22:53:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1611251, 207767, 34154, '<td valign="top">the color palette is perfect, the capture itself it great, the only thing i don''t like about this picture is the near symmetry on both sides of the frame. its too close to being perfectly symmetrical but not different enough to be non-symmetrical, really not a huge deal and is a really nitpicky and overanalytical take on the photo, but makes it an "incredibly great" photo instead of an "incredibly perfect" photo for me. great shot and i love your portfolio</td>', 'the color palette is perfect, the capture itself it great, the only thing i don''t like about this picture is the near symmetry on both sides of the frame. its too close to being perfectly symmetrical but not different enough to be non-symmetrical, really not a huge deal and is a really nitpicky and overanalytical take on the photo, but makes it an "incredibly great" photo instead of an "incredibly perfect" photo for me. great shot and i love your portfolio', '2005-08-15 02:28:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1614963, 207619, 11793, '<td valign="top">wow - amazing !  enough said.<br/></td>', 'wow - amazing !  enough said.', '2005-08-16 16:13:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1617127, 206345, 42265, '<td valign="top">dude, the bench looks totally painted in there...damn, that''s crazy looking! wow...the sky looks real, where as everything else has a "dream like" look to it.  I really like how well this whole pictures "works." wicked!</td>', 'dude, the bench looks totally painted in there...damn, that''s crazy looking! wow...the sky looks real, where as everything else has a "dream like" look to it.  I really like how well this whole pictures "works." wicked!', '2005-08-17 07:50:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1619638, 208539, 37719, '<td valign="top">Having ridden wooden roller coasters as a child, this was a very reminiscent shot.  I grew up near Coney Island and rode that roller coaster countless times.  I can just hear the screams from the riders looking at this photo.  Nice job!  Well done!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-19 10:36:51.</i></td>', 'Having ridden wooden roller coasters as a child, this was a very reminiscent shot.  I grew up near Coney Island and rode that roller coaster countless times.  I can just hear the screams from the riders looking at this photo.  Nice job!  Well done!', '2005-08-17 21:13:00.000000', '2005-08-19 11:36:51.000000', 0),
(1620941, 208520, 37719, '<td valign="top">I really liked this photo and wish it had done better.  The color pallette is perfect.  The texture detail is very nice.  Simple composition, yet enough to hold your attention.  I actually like that you left the leaf in the frame, supports the apparent age of the gate.  Well done!</td>', 'I really liked this photo and wish it had done better.  The color pallette is perfect.  The texture detail is very nice.  Simple composition, yet enough to hold your attention.  I actually like that you left the leaf in the frame, supports the apparent age of the gate.  Well done!', '2005-08-18 10:48:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1625333, 208560, 14986, '<td valign="top">Good use of desat.  His expression, the wind against his hair, and even the choice of the instrument he''s playing just gives this a classy look.  Very well done.  I especially like that this was outside.  Just don''t see this kind of instrument against that background very often.</td>', 'Good use of desat.  His expression, the wind against his hair, and even the choice of the instrument he''s playing just gives this a classy look.  Very well done.  I especially like that this was outside.  Just don''t see this kind of instrument against that background very often.', '2005-08-20 00:38:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1627176, 208322, 27812, '<td valign="top">Reminds me so much of Campsbay, Cape Town South Africa. Very nice colors, excellent composition!</td>', 'Reminds me so much of Campsbay, Cape Town South Africa. Very nice colors, excellent composition!', '2005-08-20 23:13:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1632107, 206854, 41098, '<td valign="top">I love this photo... really brings back memories of my own treehouse. Love it.</td>', 'I love this photo... really brings back memories of my own treehouse. Love it.', '2005-08-22 16:16:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1632180, 208079, 41098, '<td valign="top">I am glad to see a simple shot from you. (You seem to lean towards busy). I think it needs some sharpening or better focus and perhaps b/w? I love the off center though, good capture.</td>', 'I am glad to see a simple shot from you. (You seem to lean towards busy). I think it needs some sharpening or better focus and perhaps b/w? I love the off center though, good capture.', '2005-08-22 16:33:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1642699, 208560, 35739, '<td valign="top">This image is very nice.  I like the desat you did here. Great photo!!!!<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-24 22:00:26.</i></td>', 'This image is very nice.  I like the desat you did here. Great photo!!!!', '2005-08-24 22:59:23.000000', '2005-08-24 23:00:26.000000', 0),
(1646558, 208558, 17507, '<td valign="top">I can''t believe that 5 is the peak of your score curve! I''m amazed that so many people couldn''t be bothered to move the cursor up to "6"... and why 10 people hit below 4 is just a mystery. It''s a nice piece of work, and for those that think it''s too much woodwork and not enough photography are just blockheads :P</td>', 'I can''t believe that 5 is the peak of your score curve! I''m amazed that so many people couldn''t be bothered to move the cursor up to "6"... and why 10 people hit below 4 is just a mystery. It''s a nice piece of work, and for those that think it''s too much woodwork and not enough photography are just blockheads :P', '2005-08-26 00:40:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1658091, 207643, 34659, '<td valign="top">Not being a big cat fan myself, I am surprised at how much I like this image.  It''s very creative and unique.  I love the effects of the frame and 3D flowers.  My only very minor criticism is that because the flowers appear to be so 3D, it makes the cats themselves seem much more 2D.  And let me explain what I mean - I don''t think it''s the effect that''s creating this, I think it''s more the actual processing of the cats &amp; background themselves.  There appears to be marked edges around the cats that seem flat.  Perhaps a very small amount of blending brush and/or shadows on the edges of the cats would help support the 3D effect already in place a bit more.  Hope I don''t sound like I''m just rambling (which I tend to do).  Bottom line - very cool shot &amp; a surprisingly (for me) appealing image.</td>', 'Not being a big cat fan myself, I am surprised at how much I like this image.  It''s very creative and unique.  I love the effects of the frame and 3D flowers.  My only very minor criticism is that because the flowers appear to be so 3D, it makes the cats themselves seem much more 2D.  And let me explain what I mean - I don''t think it''s the effect that''s creating this, I think it''s more the actual processing of the cats & background themselves.  There appears to be marked edges around the cats that seem flat.  Perhaps a very small amount of blending brush and/or shadows on the edges of the cats would help support the 3D effect already in place a bit more.  Hope I don''t sound like I''m just rambling (which I tend to do).  Bottom line - very cool shot & a surprisingly (for me) appealing image.', '2005-08-30 14:57:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1665654, 208676, 36429, '<td valign="top">This is such a nice b&amp;w! I really like how composition abstract5s to make you ask questions, and the dof part explains. Nice story.</td>', 'This is such a nice b&w! I really like how composition abstract5s to make you ask questions, and the dof part explains. Nice story.', '2005-09-01 11:18:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1668902, 208515, 41918, '<td valign="top">I would question the need for a chisel and book on woodwork as a backdrop to the photo - maybe a bench instead?<br/> <br/>The focus is good - although I can''t help wondering what it would do to the image if the inside of the spoon was in focus instead...<br/> <br/>Depite all that - cracking photo!</td>', 'I would question the need for a chisel and book on woodwork as a backdrop to the photo - maybe a bench instead? The focus is good - although I can''t help wondering what it would do to the image if the inside of the spoon was in focus instead... Depite all that - cracking photo!', '2005-09-02 13:11:02.000000', NULL, 0),
